            <ArticleTitle>Characterization of β-d-N4-Hydroxycytidine as a Novel Inhibitor of Chikungunya Virus.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">e02395-16</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1128/AAC.02395-16</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chikungunya virus (CHIKV) represents a reemerging global threat to human health. Recent outbreaks across Asia, Europe, Africa, and the Caribbean have prompted renewed scientific interest in this mosquito-borne alphavirus. There are currently no vaccines against CHIKV, and treatment has been limited to nonspecific antiviral agents, with suboptimal outcomes. Herein, we have identified β-d-N4-hydroxycytidine (NHC) as a novel inhibitor of CHIKV. NHC behaves as a pyrimidine ribonucleoside and selectively inhibits CHIKV replication in cell culture.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright © 2017 American Society for Microbiology.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
